============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-Pi space along which the
  pore fraction is preserved: simultaneously rescaling the
  dimensionless groups along g keeps the LPBF physics invariant.

  Generator 1:
    Pi1 x exp(-0.420*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.867*eps), Pi3 x exp(+0.149*eps), Pi4 x exp(+0.140*eps), Pi5 x exp(+0.103*eps), Pi6 x exp(-0.144*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi2 while decrease Pi1, increase Pi3, increase Pi4, increase Pi5, decrease Pi6
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    Pi1 x exp(+0.467*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.149*eps), Pi3 x exp(+0.835*eps), Pi4 x exp(-0.155*eps), Pi5 x exp(-0.115*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.160*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi3 while increase Pi1, increase Pi2, decrease Pi4, decrease Pi5, increase Pi6
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    Pi1 x exp(+0.439*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.140*eps), Pi3 x exp(-0.155*eps), Pi4 x exp(+0.854*eps), Pi5 x exp(-0.108*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.150*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi4 while increase Pi1, increase Pi2, decrease Pi3, decrease Pi5, increase Pi6
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 4:
    Pi1 x exp(+0.324*eps), Pi2 x exp(+0.103*eps), Pi3 x exp(-0.115*eps), Pi4 x exp(-0.108*eps), Pi5 x exp(+0.921*eps), Pi6 x exp(+0.111*eps)
    Meaning: increase Pi5 while increase Pi1, increase Pi2, decrease Pi3, decrease Pi4, increase Pi6
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 5:
